        </table-wrap>
        <p>
<bold>Frequency, Intensity, Time, Type, Volume, Progression Principle&#x000a0;</bold>
</p>
        <p>The FITT-VP principle (frequency, intensity, time, type, volume, progression) provides a systematic framework for developing individualized exercise prescriptions (see <bold>Table 8</bold>). The American College of Sports Medicine recommends at least 150 minutes of physical activity per week to promote and maintain weight loss, but advises that 200 to 300 minutes per week&#x000a0;is more effective in maintaining weight loss.<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="article-179694.r12">[12]</xref></p>
        <table-wrap id="article-179694.table9" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <title>Table 8.&#x000a0;FITT-VP Exercise Prescription Framework</title>
          </caption>
