<p>8 to 10 varied</p>
</td>
                <td style="height: 35px;" rowspan="1" colspan="1">
<p>10 to 12 specialized</p>
</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </table-wrap>
        <p>Key considerations for successful implementation of resistance training programs include:</p>
        <list list-type="bullet">
          <list-item>
            <p>Prioritize compound movements that work multiple muscle groups.</p>
          </list-item>
          <list-item>
            <p>Progress gradually to prevent injury and ensure adherence to the plan.</p>
          </list-item>
          <list-item>
            <p>Include exercises for both the upper and lower body in each session.</p>
          </list-item>
          <list-item>
            <p>Emphasize proper form over heavy weights, especially in the initial stages.</p>
          </list-item>
          <list-item>
            <p>Combine with adequate protein intake (1.2&#x02013;1.6 g/kg body weight).</p>
          </list-item>
        </list>
        <p>
<bold>Addressing Exercise Barriers and Promoting Adherence</bold>
</p>
        <p>Clinicians can use various strategies to help patients adhere to prescribed exercise programs (see&#x000a0;<bold>Table 10</bold>).</p>
        <table-wrap id="article-179694.table11" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <title>Table 10. Exercise Barriers and Evidence-Based Solutions</title>
          </caption>
          <table style="width: 800px;" border="1" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="5">
